 "text": "**Digest 2026-10-14 UTC** · #cd-tracker (dev, 225 tickets) · since 2026-10-14\n\n**Summary**\n• AUD-38: tier A resumed; 19 of 80 runs are now ok. Then the OpenAI account ran out of credits, and 61 runs were refused within seconds (HTTP 429 insufficient_quota) and recorded as agent failures. About $33 of tier A is left; $12.21 spent so far.\n• INF-09 (amendment 2, operational): a billing refusal now stops a run as aborted_quota, resumable from its recorded answers, and halts the batch at the first one. The 61 runs resume with the same command once credits are added.\n\n**Done** (3)\n• ✅ DLV-04 Q1 refinement research: a refinement step that never falls below its own algorithm on…\n• ✅ INF-09 Provider quota exhaustion is an infrastructure stop, not an agent failure\n• ✅ TGT-09 Never below the system's own data-only output\n\n**New** (1)\n• ✅ INF-09 Provider quota exhaustion is an infrastructure stop, not an agent failure\n\n**Due in the next 14 days**\n• 2026-10-16 CRS-07 Decision gate G1\n• 2026-10-19 CRS-01 TA check-in 1 (TA: Nate)\n• 2026-10-20 BND-03 Paper and code audit: headline claims, methods text, untouched modules…\n• 2026-10-22 BND-02 Primary sources: literature re-reads, deep reads, method choices\n• 2026-10-24 BND-06 Remaining baselines, order sensitivity, scoreboard package (no LLM)\n• 2026-10-24 BND-08 LIVE: Causal-Copilot on CausalArena's named scenarios (old bundle 2)\n• 2026-10-28 BND-10 Refinement v1: held-out test\n\nTotals: ✅ 120 · 👀 16 · ⏳ 58 · 🔴 2 · 🔵 29",
